# SYNOPSIS

```usage
iconsgen output.swift storyboard.html
```

# DESCRIPTION

`iconsgen` reads the icon sheet of a storyboard, the `<symbol>` elements of `docs/design/shell-storyboard.html` in the tree, and writes UICore's table of them to <output.swift> (`ui/core/lib/generated/IconSheet.swift`).
Each icon is its elements in paint order, each a path in the sheet's 32-unit view box, with transforms applied, arcs and ellipses as cubic curves, and y down, and with its fill, a horizontal gradient's far end, and its stroke.

Paints are roles, as the sheet's CSS has them: the edge colour, the emblem's (the edge colour if none) and the background, each mixed at a percentage over the background.
A stroke is one pixel at any size; UICore sets its width.
The SVG it reads is the subset the sheet uses: `polygon`, `ellipse`, `path` (`M L H V C A Z`, absolute and relative), `g` with `translate`, matrix transforms, and linear gradients across an element's box.

It runs on the dev machine and is built by SwiftPM (`.build/debug/iconsgen`).
UICoreTests fails when the tree's table differs from what `iconsgen` would write.
It prints `iconsgen: <n> icons, <n> elements`.

# EXAMPLES

```rc
% .build/debug/iconsgen ui/core/lib/generated/IconSheet.swift \
	docs/design/shell-storyboard.html
```

